, "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document defines the TLS Trust Anchors extension, a mechanism\n   for relying parties to convey trusted certification authorities.  It\n   describes individual certification authorities more succinctly than\n   the TLS Certificate Authorities extension.\n\n   Additionally, to support TLS clients with many trusted certification\n   authorities, it supports a mode where servers describe their\n   available certification paths and the client selects from them.\n   Servers may describe this during connection setup, or in DNS for\n   lower latency.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids/", "expires": "2026-03-19T18:07:18Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 401895, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 29, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/401895/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2025-09-15T18:07:18Z", "title": "TLS Trust Anchor Identifiers", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document defines the TLS Trust Anchors extension, a mechanism\n   for relying parties to convey trusted certification authorities.  It\n   describes individual certification authorities more succinctly than\n   the TLS Certificate Authorities extension.\n\n   Additionally, to support TLS clients with many trusted certification\n   authorities, it supports a mode where servers describe their\n   available certification paths and the client selects from them.\n   Servers may describe this during connection setup, or in DNS for\n   lower latency.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids/", "expires": "2026-03-19T18:07:18Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 418425, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 29, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/418425/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2026-03-19T07:09:01Z", "title": "TLS Trust Anchor Identifiers", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document defines the TLS Trust Anchors extension, a mechanism\n   for relying parties to convey trusted certification authorities.  It\n   describes individual certification authorities more succinctly than\n   the TLS Certificate Authorities extension.\n\n   Additionally, to support TLS clients with many trusted certification\n   authorities, it supports a mode where servers describe their\n   available certification paths and the client selects from them.\n   Servers may describe this during connection setup, or in DNS for\n   lower latency.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids/", "expires": "2026-09-20T07:28:38Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 418435, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 29, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/418435/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2026-03-19T07:28:38Z", "title": "TLS Trust Anchor Identifiers", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document defines the TLS Trust Anchors extension, a mechanism\n   for relying parties to convey trusted certification authorities.  It\n   describes individual certification authorities more succinctly than\n   the TLS Certificate Authorities extension.\n\n   Additionally, to support TLS clients with many trusted certification\n   authorities, it supports a mode where servers describe their\n   available certification paths and the client selects from them.\n   Servers may describe this during connection setup, or in DNS for\n   lower latency.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids/", "expires": "2026-11-02T06:18:16Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 421716, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 34, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/421716/", "rev": "04", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2026-05-01T06:18:16Z", "title": "TLS Trust Anchor Identifiers", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document defines the TLS Trust Anchors extension, a mechanism\n   for a TLS client or server to select a certificate to present based\n   on the peer's trusted certification authorities.  It describes\n   certification authorities more succinctly than the TLS Certificate\n   Authorities extension.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids/", "expires": "2027-03-19T00:05:12Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 453441, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 40, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/453441/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/d